WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.542
Did you know our

00:00:01.562 --> 00:00:03.860
SALARY CYCLE is changing?

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:06.642
Here's what it means for you.

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:09.084
Up to now, it has followed

00:00:09.104 --> 00:00:11.550
a JANUARY-to-DECEMBER cycle

00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:14.635
12 months, one cycle.

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:16.094
MERIT

00:00:16.114 --> 00:00:20.350
Projected market salary movement

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:21.241
BONUS

00:00:21.261 --> 00:00:24.980
Estimated Company Performance KPIs

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:28.938
HSE  ·  FINANCE  ·  PERFORMANCE

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:32.940
Now, we're moving to a new cycle.

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:35.882
From APRIL to MARCH

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:39.756
Merit increases and promotions

00:00:39.776 --> 00:00:42.260
take effect on APRIL 1

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:45.285
That's where the cycle now begins.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:46.827
BONUS

00:00:46.847 --> 00:00:49.960
paid in the MARCH payroll

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:51.940
MARCH is the last month

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:53.412
of the cycle

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:56.960
One thing that isn't changing

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:58.929
Your PERFORMANCE APPRAISAL

00:00:58.949 --> 00:01:00.990
stays on the same schedule

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:03.111
and it will still close

00:01:03.131 --> 00:01:04.567
in DECEMBER

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:08.240
One more thing worth knowing

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:12.090
Say your merit increase is 5%

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:15.323
The implementation year covers

00:01:15.343 --> 00:01:18.100
15 MONTHS instead of 12

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:22.099
5% ÷ 12 = about 0.417%

00:01:22.119 --> 00:01:23.950
per month

00:01:24.030 --> 00:01:27.590
Multiply that by 15 months

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:31.080
and the equivalent becomes

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:32.605
6.25%

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:36.180
APRIL to MARCH

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:38.911
That's the one to remember.

00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:41.700
Why the change?

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:45.070
Closer to market best practice

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:47.321
More relevant information

00:01:47.341 --> 00:01:49.543
when we set salaries

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:52.140
If you have questions,

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:54.998
HR is ready to help.
